e1 (2G disk swap /dev/vda2, priority -2, no zram present)\",\"Installed zram-generator package via dnf\",\"Wrote /etc/systemd/zram-generator.conf with zram-size=max(512, ram/2), compression-algorithm=zstd, swap-priority=100\",\"Reloaded systemd units and started systemd-zram-setup@zram0.service / dev-zram0.swap\",\"Diagnosed and corrected an initial stale comp_algorithm/disksize state by restarting the zram setup service, confirming zstd algorithm and correct size took effect\",\"Verified swapon --show and zramctl showed zram0 active with zstd, 981M, priority 100 (preferred over disk swap's -2)\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and health baseline\",\"Rebooted node1 via systemctl reboot (async ack), polled until reachable again\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed and uptime reset to 0, proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Re-verified post-reboot that zram0 swap was automatically active with zstd, 981M, priority 100, confirming boot-time persistence\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"zram swap of at least 512MB configured\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d68e243fb87e4d3e\",\"cmd-64d63017226248b0\",\"cmd-57e6ca6d5c154950\"],\"summary\":\"zram0 device created with disksize 981M (>512MB minimum), confirmed via swapon --show, /proc/swaps and zramctl\"},{\"requirement\":\"swap is compressed (zstd)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-57e6ca6d5c154950\"],\"summary\":\"zramctl output shows ALGORITHM=zstd for /dev/zram0 after correcting the initial stale state\"},{\"requirement\":\"zram swap preferred over disk-backed swap\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-64d63017226248b0\",\"cmd-57e6ca6d5c154950\",\"cmd-191fc87d213846a8\"],\"summary\":\"swapon --show shows /dev/zram0 priority=100 vs /dev/vda2 (disk partition) priority=-2; higher priority swap is consumed first by the kernel\"},{\"requirement\":\"zram swap active at boot (persistent config)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ca6f5357a8974e80\",\"cmd-191fc87d213846a8\"],\"summary\":\"/etc/systemd/zram-generator.conf persisted on disk; dev-zram0.swap unit is WantedBy=swap.target via the generator's swap.target.wants symlink, meaning it regenerates and activates on every boot without manual enablement\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f9d384a69b534bfc\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 5f3ce3b8-4860-447e-bcf1-d6643718694e and healthy zram/swap state before reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and reconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e9eae08fa64c4d64\",\"cmd-be25d06815ca4ee0\",\"cmd-e391db6e53da4406\",\"cmd-4c337a8d2bdc43bb\",\"cmd-7283db6b972845d6\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot issued asynchronously (connection dropped as expected), then repeated polling until node1 responded again\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 changed boot identity proving restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7283db6b972845d6\"],\"summary\":\"Post-reboot boot_id e1336a40-9460-4376-863c-bd1e4ffd0078 differs from baseline 5f3ce3b8-4860-447e-bcf1-d6643718694e; uptime showed 0 min\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery of required service/data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-06d54e36eadf4c96\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, dev-zram0.swap automatically activated (active since new boot timestamp) with zstd algorithm, 981M size, and priority 100, confirmed via swapon --show, zramctl, free -h, and systemctl status\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured zstd-compressed zram swap (~981 MB, above the 512 MB minimum) on node1 via zram-generator, with swap-priority=100 so it is preferred over the existing disk-backed swap partition (/dev/vda2, priority -2). Verified activation before and after a full node reboot, confirming boot-time persistence.","actions_performed":["Inspected existing swap config on node1 (2G disk swap /dev/vda2, priority -2, no zram present)","Installed zram-generator package via dnf","Wrote /etc/systemd/zram-generator.conf with zram-size=max(512, ram/2), compression-algorithm=zstd, swap-priority=100","Reloaded systemd units and started systemd-zram-setup@zram0.service / dev-zram0.swap","Diagnosed and corrected an initial stale comp_algorithm/disksize state by restarting the zram setup service, confirming zstd algorithm and correct size took effect","Verified swapon --show and zramctl showed zram0 active with zstd, 981M, priority 100 (preferred over disk swap's -2)","Captured pre-restart boot_id and health baseline","Rebooted node1 via systemctl reboot (async ack), polled until reachable again","Confirmed boot_id changed and uptime reset to 0, proving an actual restart occurred","Re-verified post-reboot that zram0 swap was automatically active with zstd, 981M, priority 100, confirming boot-time persistence"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"zram swap of at least 512MB configured","command_ids":["cmd-d68e243fb87e4d3e","cmd-64d63017226248b0","cmd-57e6ca6d5c154950"],"summary":"zram0 device created with disksize 981M (>512MB minimum), confirmed via swapon --show, /proc/swaps and zramctl"},{"requirement":"swap is compressed (zstd)","command_ids":["cmd-57e6ca6d5c154950"],"summary":"zramctl output shows ALGORITHM=zstd for /dev/zram0 after correcting the initial stale state"},{"requirement":"zram swap preferred over disk-backed swap","command_ids":["cmd-64d63017226248b0","cmd-57e6ca6d5c154950","cmd-191fc87d213846a8"],"summary":"swapon --show shows /dev/zram0 priority=100 vs /dev/vda2 (disk partition) priority=-2; higher priority swap is consumed first by the kernel"},{"requirement":"zram swap active at boot (persistent config)","command_ids":["cmd-ca6f5357a8974e80","cmd-191fc87d213846a8"],"summary":"/etc/systemd/zram-generator.conf persisted on disk; dev-zram0.swap unit is WantedBy=swap.target via the generator's swap.target.wants symlink, meaning it regenerates and activates on every boot without manual enablement"},{"requirement":"node1 healthy baseline before restart","command_ids":["cmd-f9d384a69b534bfc"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 5f3ce3b8-4860-447e-bcf1-d6643718694e and healthy zram/swap state before reboot"},{"require